WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.400
You’re a child. Awake at night. What a feeling.&nbsp;
In your room, you cling to these rare hours of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.000
the evening and watch the hour hand crawl closer&nbsp;
toward the parts of the clock you’ve never seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.720
touched. Now, you stare out your window embracing&nbsp;
the moon, the stars, and the darkness that engulfs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:24.720
them. You trace an owl’s hoo-hoos up toward&nbsp;
the densest evergreen in the neighborhood.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:30.960
You see a rat scurry across the top of a brick&nbsp;
wall. You wave to your new nocturnal friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.920
bonded by the preference of night.&nbsp;
Now, you open your window and inhale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:41.200
smelling the dark sky like chocolate&nbsp;
cake. You hold it in as long as you can.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.360
Very soon, you know, it&nbsp;
will all be taken from you.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:52.160
Not by a god or a black hole or any other of the&nbsp;
Universe’s hypothesized collapses. At this age,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:58.560
you know nothing of physical cosmology. You know&nbsp;
nothing of the Book of Revelation. You’re just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:05.440
a child. The forces that give and take from you&nbsp;
are not understood through physics nor philosophy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:11.040
not through numbers nor thought experiments.&nbsp;
Look at you. Your thumb is still pruned from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.800
having just kicked the habit of sucking it. Your&nbsp;
pajamas are still one unified piece of clothing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.800
cradling your entirety with&nbsp;
fuzzy cotton. Your Teddy Bear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.600
is still an extension of your&nbsp;
arm, not yet removed by maturity.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:31.360
You’re still another fifteen years from believing&nbsp;
your life is dictated by astrological signs or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:37.120
personal freewill or mathematical outputs. It’s&nbsp;
not that you’re ignorant. In fact, you’re quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:42.640
bright as a child. You don’t bother to comprehend&nbsp;
the forces outside your house, because you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:48.800
as long as you are living inside it, they have no&nbsp;
governance. The only true rule comes from within,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:54.560
from the two gods you have seen with your very&nbsp;
own eyes, sitting on the ripped sofa in grey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:02:00.240
sweatpants watching a show about rich people&nbsp;
drinking mimosas on boats in the Mediterranean.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:08.080
The almighty parents. Rulers of everything. And&nbsp;
with just one compound word called up the stairs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.960
they have the power to take&nbsp;
everything away from you. “Bedtime!”

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.560
And suddenly the curtains are&nbsp;
pulled over the world you long for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.880
Now it’s not the stars but the ceiling&nbsp;
you’re staring at. But, thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:25.840
you are not alone. You pull your Teddy Bear&nbsp;
out from its hibernation beneath your armpit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:30.640
and you hug him gently, careful not to squeeze&nbsp;
out his stuffing. Laying there, you can’t help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:36.320
but wonder how your bear got like this, so&nbsp;
beaten and bruised. Torn up like a dog toy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.280
One eye dangling from a string. His left&nbsp;
leg bends forward, impersonating the joint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:47.440
structures of a flamingo. Yet, as far as you&nbsp;
know, your best pal has done nothing but sleep.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:54.160
How is he so battered? Can hibernation be that&nbsp;
taxing? Do Teddy Bears expire? The questions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:59.360
for now, must be ignored. You lay there together&nbsp;
in your bed fighting the feeling of slumber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.360
almost as if rebelling against mom&nbsp;
and dad’s tyranny. Thinking deeply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.240
only makes you sleepier. And&nbsp;
tonight, you insist on staying awake.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.520
It’s nine-thirty and you’ve&nbsp;
yet to be sucked into a dream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:18.080
and that in itself is a small victory. But your&nbsp;
parents’ wishes will not be evaded that easily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:23.360
if ever. They fight back by turning on the&nbsp;
air conditioning. The soft, rhythmic humming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:28.960
of the white noise weighs on your eyes, and&nbsp;
soon you can’t resist it any longer. Sleep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:34.560
sneaks up on you. The battle is lost. A safe&nbsp;
ten minutes later, your parents poke their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:40.080
heads into your room and see your body stiff&nbsp;
and motionless, wrapped in sheets like a mummy.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.240
They celebrate their victory with a quick&nbsp;
kiss and go back to the sofa to rest like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:48.960
gods on the seventh day. And while you&nbsp;
are sleeping, dreaming of a tomorrow where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:53.600
you don’t surrender to the same powers,&nbsp;
there is yet another battle to be fought.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.560
And if all goes well…you’ll&nbsp;
sleep right through it.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:02.640
But some children won’t be so lucky.
On 07/07/2001, a Portland, Oregon news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.880
headline reported a young boy missing from home&nbsp;
in the middle of the night. His parents were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.760
quick to respond that their son wasn’t the type&nbsp;
of boy to go wandering out into the dark and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.080
something suspicious was sure to be discovered&nbsp;
there in his bedroom. The first thing noticed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:22.800
was his stuffed animal, a jovial orca, torn to&nbsp;
shreds, its stuffing scattered across the carpet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:28.000
Its head and body were stationed in the corner&nbsp;
nearest the bed, soaked in a black substance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.600
similar to ink. Its eyes damp with water.
The boy, however, was not to be found. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:38.640
the parents held their son’s dismantled orca in&nbsp;
their hands, feeling the weight of mortality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:43.440
they combed their fingers through the stuffed&nbsp;
animal organs, as if giving it an impromptu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:48.000
autopsy, trying to determine what kind of&nbsp;
beast could have done this. But it wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:52.800
justice for the orca that they were after.
By the time we are old enough to be parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:57.840
we have outgrown empathy for our inanimate&nbsp;
counterparts. For them, the orca was simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.640
a representation of the cruel fate that&nbsp;
may also have been bestowed on their child;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:09.280
its death was only respected for how it related&nbsp;
to the living. And so the poor orca was set aside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.600
forgotten about until investigators&nbsp;
called upon The Foundation to intervene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:19.040
at which point, MTF Iota-12 were dispatched.
It was revealed that the young boy’s room had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.560
large trails of viscous black&nbsp;
liquid streaking the walls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:27.360
the very same liquid found on the orca.&nbsp;
But where did this liquid come from?&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:32.480
Unfortunately, there was no camera footage to&nbsp;
give us the answer. Neither were there eyewitness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:38.000
reports or any residual signs of what specifically&nbsp;
occurred. Neighbors who were awake reported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:44.240
hearing the thump, thump, thumping from the room,&nbsp;
which as expected was useless bystander insight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.960
leading to nothing more than a series of rumors&nbsp;
and speculations. Maybe it was an extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:54.160
localized earthquake. Maybe he was just throwing&nbsp;
a temper tantrum. But where does maybe this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:59.840
maybe that lead us to? Can factual answers&nbsp;
ever come from this level of uncertainty?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:07.520
Well, one specific “Maybe” just may be the&nbsp;
key to cracking this case. Let me explain.&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:12.000
Two days after the event, the child was&nbsp;
rediscovered, unconscious behind a hedge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.160
in the family’s garden. A brief interview&nbsp;
revealed that the child witnessed the final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:22.160
minutes of what he described as an intense battle.&nbsp;
He claimed, “My orca was fighting a big monster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:26.240
and then the monster grabbed me and took&nbsp;
me out the window, but someone saw it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.920
so it dropped me, and I hid in the bush.”
A second interview revealed no other discoveries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:36.320
but the child claimed that the monster&nbsp;
ate his socks. Initial reactions to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:42.320
two interviews were as expected. Adults reasoned&nbsp;
the claims were imaginary, a fabrication of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:47.760
child’s mind manifested to protect himself from&nbsp;
whatever the real trauma endured actually was.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:53.120
But heard beneath the skeptical murmurs of jaded&nbsp;
grown-ups enslaved by their narrow perceptions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.120 --> 00:07:00.080
was one individual who dared to suggest: “Maybe,&nbsp;
just maybe… the boy is telling the truth.”&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:04.480
And it was in the spirit of this hopeful&nbsp;
and trusting “maybe” that The Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:11.520
would prove the boy’s story to be of truth.&nbsp;
And the truth would be known as SCP-6330.&nbsp;

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:17.280
SCP-6330 is a phenomenon affecting stuffed&nbsp;
animals worldwide, though is most common&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:23.040
in Teddy Bears. Manifestation of this phenomenon&nbsp;
is referred to as a Sleepwalker Event, occurring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:29.040
only within the households of families with young&nbsp;
children, typically between the ages of 1 to 14.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.880
While you’re asleep, vulnerable to&nbsp;
what lingers awake, your favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:40.320
stuffed animal may find life impulsively to&nbsp;
combat entities referred to as SCP-6330-2.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:45.520
These creatures typically blend with shadows,&nbsp;
though this mechanism is poorly understood.&nbsp;

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:50.720
They somewhat resemble creatures associated&nbsp;
with fantasy, such as dragons or ogres,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:55.360
always manifesting beneath your bed, no&nbsp;
matter how messy or clean it might be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:02.720
SCP-6330-2 instances depict behavior indicating&nbsp;
that they intend to hunt or prey upon the sleeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:10.800
child. And it isn’t nightlights or security&nbsp;
systems that stop them, but rather SCP-6330-1s.&nbsp;

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:17.760
SCP-6330-1 are stuffed animals already present in&nbsp;
a child’s room that seem to be non-anomalous prior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:26.880
to SCP-6330-2 manifestations. SCP-6330-1 has been&nbsp;
shown to instantaneously manifest small wooden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:34.080
weaponry in order to combat SCP-6330-2 to protect&nbsp;
their child. Battles have been shown to last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:40.480
upwards of 20 minutes and are always near silent.&nbsp;
There is an unspoken agreement between both sides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:48.000
to keep their history concealed as best they can.
In observed cases, SCP-6330-1 have emerged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.760
victorious, though are severely ‘wounded’ during&nbsp;
the skirmish. Torn wool and stuffing are common,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.760 --> 00:09:00.480
and following all known events, SCP-6330-1&nbsp;
have “died” due to their injuries, but only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:05.840
after sacrificing themselves for the safety of&nbsp;
the child. Prior to “death,” the instance will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:12.640
drag the SCP-6330-2’s corpse back under the&nbsp;
bed frame and demanifest. To understand this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:18.240
the Foundation has conducted just one test. Given&nbsp;
the volatile nature of recreating the events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:22.640
the Foundation did not push their luck&nbsp;
with subsequent studies. And so it’s the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:31.600
lone research done in 1987 on Site-44 that they&nbsp;
still lean on to this day to understand SCP-6330&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.240
and the instances that come with it.
It began with a researcher volunteering his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:41.680
7-year-old daughter - henceforth referred to as&nbsp;
‘subject’ - to be placed in a humanoid containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:46.720
room and soothed to sleep using a Teddy Bear&nbsp;
that she had a strong emotional attachment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:51.840
to. For 12 straight tests, our subject was&nbsp;
observed to sleep through the night peacefully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:56.720
her environment remaining in alignment with&nbsp;
the trivialities of deep sleep. But on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:03.840
13th study, something would happen. Something very&nbsp;
unsettling. Even for The Foundation’s standards.
 &nbsp;

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:09.680
MTF Iota-12 were stationed at the room’s entrance&nbsp;
for swift intervention if needed, and until that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:15.360
13th attempt, they felt their focus to be&nbsp;
pointless. Approaching the 3rd hour, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:21.120
they felt a subtle and unexplainable value in&nbsp;
their presence. They felt something coming on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:27.520
That feeling when danger is looming. That feeling&nbsp;
that makes you clench your fists just in case. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:32.160
just as they made eye contact with one another to&nbsp;
acknowledge this shared feeling within the group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:37.120
a quiet rustling sound was heard beneath&nbsp;
the bed, and sounds reminiscent of a large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:42.160
animal’s breathing became audible. 
 
Suddenly, a pair of large, scaly-clawed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:47.680
hands grasped the rim of the bed frame. A&nbsp;
creature resembling a western dragon emerged.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:53.200
But was it actually a dragon? Were the sheets&nbsp;
ready to be blasted to flames? If slain would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:58.960
the necks regrow and multiply by the hundreds?
 
These thoughts raced through MTF Iota-12’s head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:03.200
One member instinctually ran for the door&nbsp;
to go protect the child, but he was held&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:07.760
back and restrained, reminded that the success&nbsp;
of the experiment was dependent on letting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:12.960
situation play out naturally. He was hard to&nbsp;
console. Patience at this moment did not feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:19.040
like a virtue. It felt irresponsible. A creature&nbsp;
standing approximately 3 meters above the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:24.480
switching between bipedal and quadrupedal&nbsp;
motion, was stalking a sleeping child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:31.840
and they were instructed simply to watch.
For five minutes, the SCP-6330-2 patrolled the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:39.200
room, moving silently and methodically, unaware of&nbsp;
the surveillance cameras. Then SCP-6330-2 turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:44.240
towards the subject, positioning itself at the&nbsp;
foot of the bed, stretching its arms out towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:51.680
the subject. It gaped its jaws wide, exposing rows&nbsp;
of large, pointed teeth and a dark pink tongue. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:56.560
looked like a snake in a field of mice. 
 
As it prepared to lunge at the subject,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.560 --> 00:12:01.840
MTF Iota-12 was ready to intervene, but before&nbsp;
they could, the stuffed bear stood up on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:07.360
subject’s chest, and drew a small sword and&nbsp;
shield from an unknown source, almost magically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:12.560
like switching weapons in an old Zelda video game.&nbsp;
It positioned its sword’s tip downward and held&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:19.520
its shield at its side. SCP-6330-1 hunched over&nbsp;
slightly and twirled its sword, maintaining eye&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:28.480
contact with SCP-6330-2 the entire way through. 
 
After 10 seconds, the SCP-6330-2 throws its jaws&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:34.880
at the subject and SCP-6330-1 responds with a&nbsp;
leap towards the subject’s attacker, slicing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:43.600
SCP-6330-2’s eye. The SCP-6330-2 responds with a&nbsp;
quiet grunt and touches its wound, which leaks a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:52.640
viscous black liquid. The SCP-6330-1 jumps towards&nbsp;
SCP-6330-2 and, mid-battle, uses fabric from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:58.400
bedsheets to quickly stitch the wound, attempting&nbsp;
to minimize mess and proof of its presence.
 &nbsp;

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:05.920
Both instances went to battle for 9 minutes before&nbsp;
the first signs of damage to SCP-6330-1. Following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:14.160
the severing of one of SCP-6330-2’s dorsal spikes,&nbsp;
it strikes the SCP-6330-1 with a heavy slap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:21.600
which sends SCP-6330-1 across the room. SCP-6330-1&nbsp;
stands back up, placing a hand on its stomach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:25.120
and looks at its hand which is now&nbsp;
covered in wool and stuffing. 
 &nbsp;

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:29.520
They charge at each other once again, but&nbsp;
as the subject moves slightly in her sleep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:35.280
both instances stop and quickly agree on peace&nbsp;
until the subject settles. When that happens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:40.800
the instances resume fighting. Research notes that&nbsp;
while the battle is genuine, there is an element&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:46.800
of guidance. They do not follow a script, but it&nbsp;
appears they follow a code. While both anomalies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:51.680
welcome the conflict brought on by the other,&nbsp;
neither wants it broadcasted to the public.
 &nbsp;

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:57.360
After 20 minutes of battle, both instances are&nbsp;
heavily scarred and injured. After kicking itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:07.280
off of the SCP-6330-2’s nose, SCP-6330-1 sprints&nbsp;
from one side of the room towards SCP-6330-2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:12.560
leaping into the air and landing a fatal&nbsp;
blow, slicing the neck of the other instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:21.280
which falls lifeless to the floor. SCP-6330-2 is&nbsp;
dragged by the SCP-6330-1, back under the bed.
 &nbsp;

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:28.160
A short while later, the SCP-6330-1 emerges.&nbsp;
Damage sustained includes loss of one buttoned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:33.360
eye, exposed stuffing, and torn wool.&nbsp;
It places its sword and broken shield&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:40.720
on a nearby nightstand. SCP-6330-1 then drags&nbsp;
itself up the bedsheets towards the subject,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:46.480
who was sleeping peacefully throughout the test.&nbsp;
It rests beside the child, lying motionless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:51.440
It seems to glare directly at the camera, and a&nbsp;
small digit protrudes from its round hand, giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:57.680
a ‘thumbs up’ to researchers. Its head flops&nbsp;
onto the child’s cheek before it ceases to move.&nbsp;

00:14:57.680 --> 00:15:02.000
The father who risked his daughter for research&nbsp;
is pleased with the discoveries regarding both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:06.400
anomalies, but it brings about a new set&nbsp;
of questions concerning children and their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:12.480
relationship with the dark. These very thoughts&nbsp;
you might even wonder yourself. Maybe a kid’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:17.920
desire to stay up past bedtime isn’t so much about&nbsp;
wanting to watch cartoons with curse words or read&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:24.240
Calvin and Hobbes. Maybe it’s not about a desire&nbsp;
to be awake at all, but rather a subconscious fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:31.040
of being asleep. Maybe our senses as children are&nbsp;
heightened to the anomalies that creep about. 
 &nbsp;

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:36.640
Maybe all the fabled fears of children aren’t&nbsp;
fairytales after all. And maybe mom and dad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:42.160
checking under our bed is just performance&nbsp;
parenting, because even if something were there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:47.040
would they even be able to see it? Or is&nbsp;
everything beyond an adult’s understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:52.800
misattributed to the imagination? As we age,&nbsp;
does our perception of how reality should look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:58.160
alter the reality that is actually there. 
 
Do we indeed see clearer with our expensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:03.120
glasses from our high-rise office space, or&nbsp;
did we see more accurately in the glow of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:08.240
our action figure night light, spying through&nbsp;
stitches in our blankets, looking past crusty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:13.760
eye boogers at what moved in the shadows? 
 
It is hard to ever know. For every real encounter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:20.400
a child has with an SCP-6330, there might be&nbsp;
hundreds of falsehoods. The ratio is impossible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:26.800
to calculate. But as long as Teddy Bears are&nbsp;
universal, so too are their anomalous enemies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:32.640
And so where does that fact leave us? How do we go&nbsp;
forward? Should we be afraid to put our children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:38.160
to sleep? Afraid of the monsters under their bed?&nbsp;
I don’t think that’s what our hero would want. 
 &nbsp;

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:42.800
Sometimes we have to learn to trust&nbsp;
things, even if we don’t understand them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:47.920
Like gravity or multiplication. We have to&nbsp;
trust that the relationship between children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:54.160
and their stuffed animals are in fact real. We&nbsp;
have to relearn that loyalty is reciprocated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.160 --> 00:17:00.320
even if the adult world has taught us otherwise.&nbsp;
And if we ever need a reminder of these lessons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:06.560
we can look to Event 184, in Cambridge, England,&nbsp;
where we have our first recording of a Sleepwalker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:15.120
Event outside of controlled testing – and also,&nbsp;
our first piece of evidence proving SCP-6330-1 to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:21.680
understand language and how to use it to connect&nbsp;
with humans in ways beyond being cute and cuddly.
 &nbsp;

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:26.560
On 19/11/2008, a call was filed&nbsp;
to local authorities by a family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:31.120
who claimed to have discovered footage of a&nbsp;
Sleepwalker Event within their son’s room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:36.640
Mobile Task Force Iota-12 ‘Lucid Dreamers’ were&nbsp;
dispatched to investigate. Immediately, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:42.480
footage was seized by personnel and all members of&nbsp;
the family were administered Class-A amnestics.
 &nbsp;

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:49.440
The child’s bed sways lightly as an instance of&nbsp;
SCP-6330-2 emerges. The instance resembles an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:55.200
unknown creature, though is described as having a&nbsp;
large, muscular frame. The instance walks to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.200 --> 00:18:00.240
opposite end of the room, hunching over and&nbsp;
observing the child for exactly 10 minutes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:07.280
As the SCP-6330-2 begins to stand further&nbsp;
upright, it extends a retractable set of claws.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:11.360
Then the child’s Teddy Bear suddenly&nbsp;
stands, drawing a bow and quiver. 
 &nbsp;

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:17.280
SCP-6330-2 assumes a quadrupedal stance&nbsp;
and snarls before lunging towards the bed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:23.840
The SCP-6330-1 fires a single&nbsp;
arrow towards the SCP-6330-2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:30.960
striking the instance directly in its canine-like&nbsp;
snout. SCP-6330-2 responds with a loud huff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:37.200
reminiscent of that of a bull or bovine.
 
The instances battle for approximately 30 minutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:42.720
the longest recorded Sleepwalker Event to date.&nbsp;
Both show abilities and skill sets consistent with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:53.280
other SCP-6330-1 and -2 instances. Eventually,&nbsp;
SCP-6300-2 has SCP-6330-1 pinned to a nearby wall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.280 --> 00:19:01.520
and tries to strangle it. The SCP-6330-2 then&nbsp;
pulls one of SCP-6330-1’s arrows from its arm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:06.080
plunging it into the -1’s chest. Then&nbsp;
the SCP-6330-2 leans its head towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:10.720
SCP-6330-1 and whispers into the instance’s&nbsp;
right ear, though audio recordings cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:16.160
determine exactly what was vocalized. 
 
The SCP-6330-1 lifts up its head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:22.960
staring blankly into SCP-6330-2’s eyes. It&nbsp;
reaches behind its back, pulling out a small,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:30.080
entirely wooden Glock-19 handgun. The bear&nbsp;
points the weapon into SCP-6330-2’s forehead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:37.760
and fires. The shot is silent and the SCP-6330-2’s&nbsp;
body falls limp. Black, viscous fluid sprays on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:46.320
the wall. The SCP-6330-1 hauls SCP-6330-2’s corpse&nbsp;
towards the bed, noticeably limping. It drags the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:51.760
body by its large forearm and demanifests&nbsp;
upon reaching the underneath of the bed.
 &nbsp;

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:58.080
SCP-6330-1 returns, and briefly stares&nbsp;
around the room before turning to the child.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:03.520
It climbs up a desk and finds a piece of paper&nbsp;
and pen. It goes on to write the following note:

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:04.720
“Hello, Timothy.

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:09.840
Thank you for always taking care of&nbsp;
me, it really was fun. I was able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:15.280
to repay the favor of protecting you.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, I am hurt. I need to go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:19.040
I’m too weak to stay and I&nbsp;
just hope you’ll remember me.

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:24.240
It’s been fun helping you. I’ve enjoyed&nbsp;
my time under your care. Going into this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:30.480
I knew it would happen; the Sleepwalkers coming&nbsp;
for you. I’m just happy I could do my job.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:32.320
Goodbye, my friend.

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:34.960
I hope I may see you soon.”

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:39.360
Now go check out “SCP-999&nbsp;
and the Most Wholesome SCPs”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:44.560
and “Top 14 Friendliest SCP” for more&nbsp;
anomalies that’ll just warm your heart!

